# What `docker build` must not copy into the build context for deployment/quickstart/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile in preference to a `.dockerignore`
# at the root of the context, which is why this file is here rather than at the top of the
# repository: the quickstart owns its own exclusions and does not need to add a file to the root.
#
# The point is not tidiness. The build context is sent to the Docker daemon before anything runs;
# including `out/` (a full Mill build tree, often gigabytes) or `node_modules/` would make the
# newcomer wait through a large upload for files the build then ignores.

out/
node_modules/
.git/
.idea/
.vscode/
.bsp/
.metals/
.bloop/
e2e/node_modules/
**/*.log
